Q: Instantiate objects at spawn points A: <p>I'm guessing that in more than one of the <code>Update()</code> calls that <code>QuestManager.questManager.RequestAcceptedQuest(1)</code> is returning true, causing <code>SpawnFlowers()</code> to run each time.</p>
<p>To fix that, you could fix the logic in the <code>QuestManager</code> to only return true one time, or a better way that makes more sense would probably be to track the &quot;work&quot; done in <code>SpawnFlower</code>.</p>
<p>In <code>SpawnFlower</code> at the top add:</p>
<pre><code>private bool _hasInitialized = false;
</code></pre>
<p>Then, in <code>SpawnFlowers()</code> set the variable:</p>
<pre><code>public void SpawnFlowers()
{
    var freeSpawnPoints = new List&lt;Transform&gt;(spawnPoints);

    // The rest of the method
    ...

    // Set this so the work wont be done more than once even though 
    _hasInitialized = true;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Then update your check in <code>Update()</code>:</p>
<pre><code>void Update()
{
    if (_hasInitialized)
    {
        return;
    }

    //InvokeRepeating (&quot;SpawnFlowers&quot;, spawnTime, spawnTime);
    if (QuestManager.questManager.RequestAcceptedQuest(1))
    {
        SpawnFlowers ();
    }
}
</code></pre>
